Commands
  set-var name expression  update a runtime option
  set-output "path"       choose the save destination
  set-map key "keys"      add a key mapping (expands in Normal mode)
  let name expression     append an integer variable
  echo value              display a string or variable
  :w                      save
  :q                      quit if there are no unsaved changes
  :q!                     quit and discard unsaved changes
  :wq                     save and quit
  :e / :we                legacy exit / save-and-exit aliases
                          (:e respects the unsaved-changes guard)
  !command                run through sh -c and show the last stdout line

Special mapping keys
  <space> <esc>/<escape> <tab> <nul>
  <cr>/<enter>/<return> <bs>/<backspace>
  <up> <down> <left> <right> <home> <end>
  <delete>/<del> <insert>/<ins>
  <pageup>/<page-up> <pagedown>/<page-down>
  <c-a> through <c-z> (also <ctrl-a> through <ctrl-z>) and <c-?>

  A mapping can run a colon command by embedding the Enter that submits it,
  e.g. set-map <c-p> ":wq" with a literal newline before the closing quote.
